values ('d3e4f5a6-7b8c-4e93-8f23-4a5b6c7d8e33', 'deviance-and-social-control', 'Deviance and Social Control', 'Deviance and Social Control examines how societies define, label, manage, punish, treat, normalize, and resist behavior considered deviant. The course centers sociological theory while integrating criminology, law, public health, psychology, media studies, and policy analysis. Students study classic theories, contemporary data, criminal justice institutions, stigma, medicalization, surveillance, moral panics, punishment, inequality, and global variations in social control.');

