  'Deviance and Social Control',
  'Deviance and Social Control examines how societies define, label, manage, punish, treat, normalize, and resist behavior considered deviant. The course centers sociological theory while integrating criminology, law, public health, psychology, media studies, and policy analysis. Students study classic theories, contemporary data, criminal justice institutions, stigma, medicalization, surveillance, moral panics, punishment, inequality, and global variations in social control.',
  $devsjson${"slug": "deviance-and-social-control", "title": "Deviance and Social Control", "description": "Deviance and Social Control examines how societies define, label, manage, punish, treat, normalize, and resist behavior considered deviant. The course centers sociological theory while integrating criminology, law, public health, psychology, media studies, and policy analysis. Students study classic theories, contemporary data, criminal justice institutions, stigma, medicalization, surveillance, moral panics, punishment, inequality, and global variations in social control.", "topics": [{"id": "4cfbffd4-869d-4db6-813b-3115d549553a", "type": "topic", "title": "Defining Deviance, Norms, and Sanctions", "description": "This opening unit establishes deviance as a social relationship between behavior, norms, audiences, and consequences. Students learn that deviance is not simply behavior that is unusual or harmful; it is behavior interpreted through rules, power, culture, and social reaction.", "children": [{"id": "c89595e7-3ea0-40f8-b552-81ad57dd76cd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Norms and normative orders", "children": [{"id": "c6561dad-0390-4f0f-8961-14174edd65c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Folkways, mores, and laws"}, {"id": "9e624fb0-c987-4d61-a357-18075ffbcdca", "type": "concept", "title": "Context-dependent norms"}, {"id": "83532fe4-75fa-4582-8f62-6d4b518f9dd7", "type": "concept", "title": "Norm conflict and pluralism"}], "description": "Students examine how formal and informal expectations define acceptable conduct across settings."}, {"id": "f549a360-ad90-4732-ad52-436bc0a90133", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sanctions and social reaction", "children": [{"id": "d16c39c3-5a15-436c-9a2c-f877767e3044", "type": "concept", "title": "Positive and negative sanctions"}, {"id": "4e806031-f294-45f4-a4c5-1c387e8e978f", "type": "concept", "title": "Informal and formal sanctions"}, {"id": "80bd2e40-2f8b-4ea8-825f-a56c8c946f07", "type": "concept", "title": "Consequences for identity and opportunity"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces praise, stigma, exclusion, punishment, treatment, and surveillance as responses to rule-breaking."}, {"id": "3f32962b-8355-4e58-a641-8594df095631", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Relativity of deviance", "children": [{"id": "ad383965-a184-42ce-9ae2-9ea5c78796a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Historical change"}, {"id": "2b0254c9-73d7-4120-a2b0-e68bc94853ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Subcultural difference"}, {"id": "06024366-e170-4488-8aef-e27a05b2974a", "type": "concept", "title": "Power and boundary-making"}], "description": "Students learn why definitions of deviance vary across time, place, institutions, and groups."}]}, {"id": "9ad9b9a7-fd88-4b51-9308-59174dce992e", "type": "topic", "title": "The Sociological Study of Deviance and Social Control", "description": "This unit introduces deviance as a central sociological problem: how societies create rules, mark boundaries, respond to difference, and organize conformity. It also prepares students to evaluate theories and evidence rather than relying on stereotypes.", "children": [{"id": "001d019e-41eb-4186-9fae-530511f297be", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social construction and empirical inquiry", "children": [{"id": "9b90c7bc-48e1-48b8-a349-71d13876002c", "type": "concept", "title": "Claims-making"}, {"id": "a162a492-06b4-4797-844a-134d9f324e85", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutional classification"}, {"id": "6beea467-7206-435f-8dde-93554f745d40", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence versus moral assumption"}], "description": "Students learn to ask how deviance categories are made, sustained, contested, and measured."}, {"id": "c62ec988-4597-4b7e-a1ad-e7e9b5cf7f14", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Levels of analysis", "children": [{"id": "9c9b72e4-da92-43f7-a27c-82aa9376be50", "type": "concept", "title": "Micro interaction"}, {"id": "e7ab3d3e-2117-40ab-9c82-29e234ef74e1", "type": "concept", "title": "Organizations and institutions"}, {"id": "e47c5943-242a-4a3e-b8a8-6caf4595b02b", "type": "concept", "title": "Macro inequality and state power"}], "description": "This subtopic connects individual behavior with groups, organizations, communities, law, media, and political economy."}, {"id": "893c10cd-c9db-4cb6-9d2e-863324d8f96d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethics of studying deviance", "children": [{"id": "3ccd61f9-bf56-4f09-acfb-8fe8d7cb030c", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidentiality and risk"}, {"id": "73178e9d-0dba-4875-8361-164f874fd2ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Researcher positionality"}, {"id": "e0c318b2-6abf-4227-94f1-5547423990e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding harm and sensationalism"}], "description": "Students discuss how to study stigmatized groups, illegal behavior, and harmed communities responsibly."}]}, {"id": "6d310c02-b979-4ac2-9506-9dbc8b668886", "type": "topic", "title": "Functionalist Theories: Durkheim, Anomie, and Strain", "description": "Functionalist theories ask what deviance does for social order and what happens when norms, goals, and institutions fall out of alignment. Students learn why deviance can reveal the boundaries and tensions of society.", "children": [{"id": "d44990f3-f935-40a4-87f2-0c6e5178cd18", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Durkheim and the functions of deviance", "children": [{"id": "9f4ab351-6ff9-4eca-8eea-6b24a4c184d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Collective conscience"}, {"id": "637af23a-7fd7-4a11-9d0b-75104020175e", "type": "concept", "title": "Boundary maintenance"}, {"id": "a3399dcf-1f46-4b7c-856f-e2467a5a6051", "type": "concept", "title": "Deviance and innovation"}], "description": "Students examine deviance as normal, boundary-making, and sometimes a source of social change."}, {"id": "4ea8b488-935d-47ab-aac6-d31f9e541bec", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Anomie and strain", "children": [{"id": "420e13de-d112-47e7-a6ef-acfd6a4e540e", "type": "concept", "title": "Merton's strain theory"}, {"id": "37f0ddc5-47cb-4c2b-bbff-d9f5def62b84", "type": "concept", "title": "Goals and institutionalized means"}, {"id": "5ae8a1f4-3bf5-42e4-9303-4c6fe5881731", "type": "concept", "title": "Adaptation types"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces how blocked opportunities and normlessness can produce deviant adaptations."}, {"id": "de52565a-74cd-4951-958f-7ba4848ca8b3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Contemporary strain perspectives", "children": [{"id": "1d001b87-75f8-45fe-92ae-50510f3c5772", "type": "concept", "title": "General strain theory"}, {"id": "35a6773f-fda0-4d45-ae33-1d616a35d120", "type": "concept", "title": "Relative deprivation"}, {"id": "ceef9df0-a11e-4a9e-850e-e393b6400299", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutional strain"}], "description": "Students extend strain theory to stress, inequality, frustration, and coping."}]}, {"id": "ba135c8b-f3fc-465b-87d4-8c0daa6fc3e9", "type": "topic", "title": "Conflict Theories, Power, and the Making of Rules", "description": "Conflict theories shift attention from rule-breaking to rule-making. Students learn to ask who has the power to define deviance, whose harms are criminalized, and whose misconduct is normalized or protected.", "children": [{"id": "670b0a62-ff1a-48b8-810f-1ee3be49f823", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Power and legal classification", "children": [{"id": "9bc35ab3-981f-40e1-8ca1-59020551de0a", "type": "concept", "title": "Lawmaking and enforcement"}, {"id": "cbf4f131-c0a9-4bb3-9312-efaceea415eb", "type": "concept", "title": "Moral regulation"}, {"id": "aecca306-a931-49d0-9e39-61c6ce0c0166", "type": "concept", "title": "Selective criminalization"}], "description": "Students examine law as a social product shaped by conflict, interest, ideology, and institutional power."}, {"id": "2f422eb7-40b3-49bd-94b8-e1ea55fe6682", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inequality and social control", "children": [{"id": "45ea5d1c-595c-4513-93a1-005b00b4f7cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Differential enforcement"}, {"id": "13aeca3f-bcd4-47a6-9a7b-c695a35d88f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Criminalization of poverty"}, {"id": "c346217b-7910-4cbd-b5aa-65b06cb9e291", "type": "concept", "title": "Control of marginalized groups"}], "description": "This subtopic connects control institutions to class, race, gender, citizenship, disability, and sexuality."}, {"id": "3e7754bd-688b-41ea-9f34-da18641d9399", "type": "subtopic", "title": "White-collar, corporate, and state deviance", "children": [{"id": "a1f7ec75-2275-4829-929d-4170415babc1", "type": "concept", "title": "Corporate crime"}, {"id": "70eee7aa-62aa-4683-b8bf-85ad64cb3d2b", "type": "concept", "title": "State crime and human rights"}, {"id": "b830279a-2f68-483d-845e-27c6d92ee3de", "type": "concept", "title": "Regulatory capture and impunity"}], "description": "Students study powerful actors whose harmful actions may be treated differently from street-level deviance."}]}, {"id": "755c2aac-adef-47eb-8597-f04b05e64ca6", "type": "topic", "title": "Symbolic Interaction, Labeling, and Stigma", "description": "Interactionist theories show how deviance emerges through meanings, labels, identities, and social reactions. This unit is central for understanding stigma, moral entrepreneurship, and the consequences of being marked deviant.", "children": [{"id": "e8294c2f-0f7c-4e67-b5ec-5d348a750eeb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Labeling theory", "children": [{"id": "f5fa65f4-1b36-40bf-a6ab-047449c70d2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary and secondary deviance"}, {"id": "f7abfd10-2eea-47ea-badb-7e99c848fabf", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-fulfilling prophecy"}, {"id": "0d97ebe3-94a3-498f-85d5-7f31bcfce640", "type": "concept", "title": "Deviant careers"}], "description": "Students learn how labels can amplify deviance by altering identity, opportunity, surveillance, and social treatment."}, {"id": "29f52d11-93f7-4830-83c3-d99177958ed8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Stigma and identity management", "children": [{"id": "5864e329-331c-4792-8ea7-975f5e1d9cca", "type": "concept", "title": "Discredited and discreditable identities"}, {"id": "b89405aa-5bcb-4641-a42a-b49781ff6b01", "type": "concept", "title": "Passing and covering"}, {"id": "4d715493-7c8f-415e-b62b-b4f17b644405", "type": "concept", "title": "Courtesy stigma"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces stigma as a social process that shapes interaction, disclosure, passing, covering, and resistance."}, {"id": "7011101a-1e07-4da6-bfa7-9b6fd4fda882", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Moral entrepreneurs and claims-making", "children": [{"id": "05ed6268-ee84-4e3f-8646-4500eeeaaecf", "type": "concept", "title": "Rule creators and rule enforcers"}, {"id": "6534473b-a5d5-4e9d-9cda-9004cbc3e181", "type": "concept", "title": "Moral campaigns"}, {"id": "6b44bac2-ce41-4e92-a8ed-8318d40962cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Counterclaims and resistance"}], "description": "Students study how individuals, groups, media, and institutions campaign to define behaviors or populations as problematic."}]}, {"id": "c79bf868-c352-4216-aa04-a0ff66deedd1", "type": "topic", "title": "Informal Social Control: Families, Peers, Schools, Workplaces, and Communities", "description": "Not all social control happens through law. This unit examines everyday mechanisms that encourage conformity, punish difference, or reproduce inequality before formal institutions ever intervene.", "children": [{"id": "3aab25da-84c8-4c3e-a2d1-2cca8246178e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Socialization and conformity", "children": [{"id": "debe222d-5437-4a6d-b3b0-5a22189751f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Internalization of norms"}, {"id": "0ea407a3-2a43-4068-b449-3db2f7f9f466", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer pressure and belonging"}, {"id": "05c83008-2b08-4703-a796-cc069ecccd65", "type": "concept", "title": "Conformity and identity"}], "description": "Students examine how norms are learned through family, school, religion, peers, work, and community life."}, {"id": "358cb721-c854-423c-87e3-f108ab6e4ac2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Informal sanctions and exclusion", "children": [{"id": "8d4c9804-277d-4893-b8f9-e20eb7a5f0da", "type": "concept", "title": "Shame and embarrassment"}, {"id": "876cb5a7-e4a9-46ca-b546-6f54c7a3396a", "type": "concept", "title": "Status loss"}, {"id": "5e443eef-449e-43b4-aee3-612d728c292b", "type": "concept", "title": "Community exclusion"}], "description": "This subtopic explores gossip, ridicule, shaming, ostracism, discipline, and reputational control."}, {"id": "d254ca6d-9e4e-4b21-91e0-c9a1dfcb8467", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Community control and collective efficacy", "children": [{"id": "2a460b4c-c2c5-4964-89d8-2f10fc70b0f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Neighborhood social control"}, {"id": "e1966034-b6b0-4cb4-adc1-3013fc76626d", "type": "concept", "title": "Collective efficacy"}, {"id": "6a052fce-85a6-4a81-af42-a3ef633058de", "type": "concept", "title": "Informal justice and restorative practices"}], "description": "Students learn how social ties and shared expectations can reduce harm or intensify surveillance."}]}, {"id": "4956ac9f-6a77-47ef-9441-130090686368", "type": "topic", "title": "Formal Social Control: Law, Bureaucracy, and Institutions", "description": "Formal social control includes rules, agencies, records, sanctions, professional authority, and bureaucratic procedures. Students learn how institutions transform behavior into cases, diagnoses, violations, and punishments.", "children": [{"id": "b72d0c4c-7a50-4b1f-835b-611a4062b849", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Law and legal authority", "children": [{"id": "b5316109-7145-4a89-a00b-0a337c217b57", "type": "concept", "title": "Criminalization and decriminalization"}, {"id": "ccd59723-2c8f-458a-856d-2ccdf2a216ae", "type": "concept", "title": "Civil regulation"}, {"id": "62d5eec3-bcab-433b-800d-e5f5ead2f762", "type": "concept", "title": "Administrative control"}], "description": "Students examine the role of criminal, civil, administrative, and regulatory law in defining and controlling deviance."}, {"id": "03549f3c-154a-445d-9f87-9a5f67164e6a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Bureaucratic classification", "children": [{"id": "d1222e68-1243-4a94-9c14-ff96591e4824", "type": "concept", "title": "Case files and records"}, {"id": "8535f801-9a2c-4f0e-873b-65275a1d9b1f", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk categories"}, {"id": "ba483e5f-217b-4978-863f-2019a2daf093", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutional discretion"}], "description": "This subtopic shows how institutions classify people through files, records, categories, and eligibility rules."}, {"id": "0b32ef6a-f082-453f-88fa-5c9fa47585da", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Treatment, discipline, and punishment", "children": [{"id": "fd681ba2-fb9d-4ef7-a8d7-aa51d2d4f7af", "type": "concept", "title": "Medicalization"}, {"id": "cf0fff36-9305-4dd1-8a00-8c5eebe752e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Disciplinary power"}, {"id": "30d11c64-ad56-4db5-874e-bcbb86ce3c46", "type": "concept", "title": "Punitive and rehabilitative models"}], "description": "Students compare medical, therapeutic, educational, correctional, and managerial responses to deviance."}]}, {"id": "e491958f-f0da-458e-a572-aa953fee09f5", "type": "topic", "title": "Crime, Criminalization, and the Criminal Justice System", "description": "Crime is a major but not exclusive form of deviance. This unit connects sociological theories of deviance to criminal law, police, courts, corrections, and reform debates.", "children": [{"id": "6265564e-f1f2-4ef7-a1af-5f319c5f877f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Crime as a legal and social category", "children": [{"id": "5c7a330a-b7e6-4162-936f-395b1102a990", "type": "concept", "title": "Mala in se and mala prohibita"}, {"id": "bc7afc6b-a022-436a-aef5-070eee9ed3e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Harm and victimization"}, {"id": "70a12448-c557-49b6-aa2a-8d1e38ae8308", "type": "concept", "title": "Criminalization processes"}], "description": "Students distinguish legal definitions of crime from sociological definitions of harm, deviance, and social reaction."}, {"id": "828e63bc-43f5-4404-bb84-ffde5e368071", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Police, courts, and corrections", "children": [{"id": "e856c3dc-0a33-404e-b0ac-ab6a35ad5c8a", "type": "concept", "title": "Police discretion"}, {"id": "eb002c6e-aafa-4377-a8bb-8ed9f03bba3e", "type": "concept", "title": "Prosecution and plea bargaining"}, {"id": "faa09fc0-54e5-4a5b-9b6d-d77654bebeda", "type": "concept", "title": "Jails, prisons, probation, and parole"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces the major institutions that process criminalized behavior."}, {"id": "a2e581b1-f7e1-4e20-ae67-74bb716d932e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Criminal justice policy models", "children": [{"id": "12872f44-c2cd-47bd-93d9-82484020a751", "type": "concept", "title": "Due process versus crime control"}, {"id": "d74a4b4c-04a0-41b2-ab0a-027b8f41c964", "type": "concept", "title": "Restorative justice"}, {"id": "fef8364e-03f4-41ae-b607-bd3497979d79", "type": "concept", "title": "Reform and abolition debates"}], "description": "Students compare due process, crime control, restorative, abolitionist, and public health approaches."}]}, {"id": "7b1bfb7c-7778-420f-83fa-6af3d12485d6", "type": "topic", "title": "Measuring Deviance and Crime", "description": "A world-class course must teach students how deviance and crime are counted, missed, distorted, and interpreted. This unit builds empirical literacy for official data, surveys, ethnography, and mixed-method evidence.", "children": [{"id": "e1e42ef2-2370-4726-87bf-b0682522146f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Official statistics and administrative data", "children": [{"id": "83dd98f5-7aac-4c86-9c27-d40b6292907a", "type": "concept", "title": "UCR/NIBRS"}, {"id": "cebdfad8-90b4-4079-b6fc-e9b23c4dcede", "type": "concept", "title": "Arrest and conviction data"}, {"id": "0fa9dbdc-0284-485d-a45a-d10181be74b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Administrative bias"}], "description": "Students learn how police reports, court records, corrections data, and agency statistics are produced and limited."}, {"id": "8690d764-4c18-4ec2-bb08-85ad4d6aa81f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Victimization and self-report surveys", "children": [{"id": "d00cec53-af7c-44a5-a048-66876b519254", "type": "concept", "title": "NCVS and victimization surveys"}, {"id": "b32deb65-4bec-4e32-befd-d1e3a0789802", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-report delinquency studies"}, {"id": "0768584c-2dee-4999-a829-727a20366cd1", "type": "concept", "title": "Sampling and reporting bias"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces survey-based approaches that capture experiences often missing from official records."}, {"id": "95d2c0fc-5910-41c7-826c-1afd20dbeab3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Qualitative and ethnographic evidence", "children": [{"id": "57ea3220-63ef-406f-ba19-1642ee8cab58", "type": "concept", "title": "Field access and ethics"}, {"id": "95f3356e-1691-4ea2-a3f2-c6021aa567d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Thick description"}, {"id": "ff4f0ea2-4df2-4579-9440-f1c348135d93", "type": "concept", "title": "Triangulation"}], "description": "Students examine how interviews, observation, archival work, and case studies reveal meanings and institutions."}]}, {"id": "66811ae7-aeaa-4f27-8d03-4683362fce36", "type": "topic", "title": "Policing, Surveillance, and Everyday Regulation", "description": "This unit examines policing as both a formal institution and a broader social practice of monitoring, sorting, and regulating people. Students analyze discretion, technology, legitimacy, and accountability.", "children": [{"id": "eaf33ab6-4e2c-42f2-aa59-e0057d8b4edf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Police discretion and legitimacy", "children": [{"id": "1cda4215-5e8e-4d4a-a1bd-a771f6167ac7", "type": "concept", "title": "Discretion and selective enforcement"}, {"id": "cc6955b0-b31c-4851-8118-4eb96845d120", "type": "concept", "title": "Procedural justice"}, {"id": "678de623-71c2-436c-b5a6-093c13c7a56b", "type": "concept", "title": "Community trust"}], "description": "Students study how officers and agencies decide whom to stop, search, warn, arrest, or refer."}, {"id": "a980cd0e-b539-4b4e-8cc5-3c4a9f62a5ad", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Surveillance and data power", "children": [{"id": "9d92197b-1c5f-4f8b-9dae-7a3d4762a4dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk assessment"}, {"id": "e4ea058f-d69e-4b21-9d33-524da6998850", "type": "concept", "title": "Predictive policing"}, {"id": "f0232883-85af-42ee-9334-fb9dcf011950", "type": "concept", "title": "Privacy and civil liberties"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces cameras, databases, predictive tools, platform monitoring, workplace surveillance, and algorithmic control."}, {"id": "da42dbe5-3654-4aa7-b379-fa2d6233b3d6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Accountability and reform", "children": [{"id": "b5a5e0c6-27c5-4a4e-a407-4acf655d448f", "type": "concept", "title": "Use-of-force policy"}, {"id": "7726a347-1e66-420b-aa02-e5a3d83bba13", "type": "concept", "title": "Civilian oversight"}, {"id": "2c351f13-1669-4194-947f-32dffbf350f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Alternative response models"}], "description": "Students compare policy responses to misconduct, over-policing, under-protection, and public safety demands."}]}, {"id": "82a661b7-5f73-40f5-ab6e-2285c7cb51f5", "type": "topic", "title": "Punishment, Corrections, and Mass Incarceration", "description": "Punishment reveals what societies value, fear, and are willing to do in the name of order. This unit studies theories of punishment, correctional institutions, collateral consequences, and reform.", "children": [{"id": "1d2c7f01-1920-4a8b-922a-0fb278bf719f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Theories of punishment", "children": [{"id": "37440312-959f-4f02-b9d9-235fa0d0b817", "type": "concept", "title": "Retribution and proportionality"}, {"id": "b9145a02-db8e-436d-bde0-640f96d1a535", "type": "concept", "title": "General and specific deterrence"}, {"id": "2f8c353e-9e40-4aaf-a66f-6874fb48e543", "type": "concept", "title": "Rehabilitation and desistance"}], "description": "Students compare retribution, deterrence, incapacitation, rehabilitation, restorative justice, and reintegration."}, {"id": "d0f5e1b6-c187-415b-ad8a-285ed38f2638", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Correctional institutions and supervision", "children": [{"id": "c6fb9dd3-d8bb-4703-8e47-f363d40de6e1", "type": "concept", "title": "Prison life and institutionalization"}, {"id": "216777ba-0779-41f3-8403-dd0ca12d1743", "type": "concept", "title": "Probation and parole"}, {"id": "38fe6ec6-ce43-4cd2-80df-210f22004d24", "type": "concept", "title": "Reentry and collateral consequences"}], "description": "This subtopic examines jails, prisons, probation, parole, reentry, and community corrections."}, {"id": "5ca173c5-63fb-4c24-bcbf-efcd8ba13ef9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mass incarceration and inequality", "children": [{"id": "b13bc3aa-e6a6-4be1-92bf-5a935f2b4b70", "type": "concept", "title": "War on drugs"}, {"id": "c846867b-63a1-47a2-8c48-4539739abd66", "type": "concept", "title": "Sentencing and mandatory minimums"}, {"id": "16f87389-724e-4f39-be9c-cce08e4705c1", "type": "concept", "title": "Families and communities"}], "description": "Students analyze incarceration growth, racial disparities, sentencing policy, and social consequences."}]}, {"id": "40119c7a-7975-46d1-b17e-c0581b1b5e0c", "type": "topic", "title": "Race, Class, Gender, Sexuality, and Intersectional Control", "description": "Definitions and enforcement of deviance are deeply unequal. This unit helps students analyze how social control operates through intersecting systems of race, class, gender, sexuality, immigration status, disability, and age.", "children": [{"id": "78366d19-aef4-4774-a994-2255e9e7f230", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Racialization and criminalization", "children": [{"id": "93ab243f-c317-47d3-abf6-b38c95aeb4dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Racial profiling"}, {"id": "686762be-01cb-4ded-bcda-b720e6be492e", "type": "concept", "title": "Racial threat theory"}, {"id": "1d7bce50-c00a-4c68-a769-3fe6db44d8aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Disparities and discrimination"}], "description": "Students study how racial categories and stereotypes shape policing, punishment, media, and public fear."}, {"id": "2942a1e9-30f2-4f72-b7a4-5e5c3c078933", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gender, sexuality, and respectability", "children": [{"id": "a26f090e-3878-445b-9714-805e2f3ca9b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Double standards"}, {"id": "7d96f04b-a480-4893-91ce-71d811f5d4a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Queer criminalization and resistance"}, {"id": "75c18125-c94b-4d91-b236-90dd5c887236", "type": "concept", "title": "Respectability politics"}], "description": "This subtopic examines how bodies, sexuality, family forms, and gender expression are normalized or controlled."}, {"id": "8207779d-0de6-409d-b7bf-a8346f4cb62b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Class, poverty, and disorder", "children": [{"id": "ccd2f012-9a39-4f0a-8b0b-99072c6a4e16", "type": "concept", "title": "Broken windows debates"}, {"id": "94319009-98dc-4a8c-b9d3-fea56cfa2639", "type": "concept", "title": "Criminalization of homelessness"}, {"id": "e1c7acb5-c8bd-4cbd-8a03-84e051053bee", "type": "concept", "title": "Fines, fees, and debt"}], "description": "Students analyze how poverty, homelessness, welfare, public space, and disorder become targets of regulation."}]}, {"id": "69467217-4059-4bcd-80d7-104c5f817e40", "type": "topic", "title": "Mental Illness, Disability, Medicalization, and Stigma", "description": "This unit examines how mental illness and disability can be framed as deviance, disease, risk, difference, or rights-based identity. Students learn to analyze stigma without reducing people to labels.", "children": [{"id": "177e9cc3-d555-45e3-873a-07f31b95c8cf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Medicalization and diagnosis", "children": [{"id": "4a014fcb-d94f-4d1b-aca2-ad2ca75d84f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Medicalization and demedicalization"}, {"id": "53f49d1b-25b5-494d-970b-d405f40c4867", "type": "concept", "title": "DSM and classification"}, {"id": "678440c3-f270-4be2-8afd-2ebf3e716f77", "type": "concept", "title": "Treatment versus control"}], "description": "Students study how behaviors and experiences become medical categories and how diagnosis can help or harm."}, {"id": "3ec0c2fa-8014-47fb-88cc-5a77e7ec69b4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Stigma and social exclusion", "children": [{"id": "b3a7b9d8-ef43-49f7-b2ed-5c8f068d4344", "type": "concept", "title": "Public stigma"}, {"id": "3711768d-6f0a-4c90-8d55-66c3022d5489", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-stigma"}, {"id": "841682f5-6d9b-4849-bef0-ebe61d751390", "type": "concept", "title": "Structural stigma"}], "description": "This subtopic connects mental illness and disability stigma to employment, housing, policing, healthcare, and family life."}, {"id": "f62a786f-7bbf-4975-83f8-452e60283c2b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Crisis response and institutional alternatives", "children": [{"id": "900f2159-1688-4c3f-9446-2a0526c294dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Crisis intervention"}, {"id": "5a85a412-568e-4d29-b3d9-72101d673f44", "type": "concept", "title": "Diversion and problem-solving courts"}, {"id": "eca72d6e-3534-4725-9221-572b1309866f", "type": "concept", "title": "Community-based support"}], "description": "Students compare criminal justice, clinical, community, and peer-support responses to crisis."}]}, {"id": "e9f235a2-01b0-4ccb-9ce1-e04a9283194d", "type": "topic", "title": "Substance Use, Addiction, Moral Panics, and Public Health", "description": "Substance use is a classic site where deviance, crime, health, race, markets, and policy collide. Students analyze how societies define drugs, users, treatment, punishment, and harm reduction.", "children": [{"id": "bc60237d-e75b-4d98-98c1-b082120a08ee", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Drug scares and moral panics", "children": [{"id": "b36a548f-5e4c-49cd-87d7-d7e202beffad", "type": "concept", "title": "Moral panic cycles"}, {"id": "2ce874fe-df74-4014-ae6b-400c1b9a2ec2", "type": "concept", "title": "Racialized drug scares"}, {"id": "816f8893-4036-49af-8d1a-0cff2edcd749", "type": "concept", "title": "Media amplification"}], "description": "Students examine how public fear, media, politics, and stereotypes shape drug policy."}, {"id": "05b000f5-7a54-4ab3-8e1a-cd23e73222c9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Addiction science and social context", "children": [{"id": "ef38e8fb-d81c-4a2d-bf97-30e4872a007a", "type": "concept", "title": "Dependence and addiction"}, {"id": "5fd91bb3-34c2-4327-b669-74f445e105a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk and protective factors"}, {"id": "dc699307-c065-4d6b-b2dd-5b91c3687519", "type": "concept", "title": "Co-occurring conditions"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces substance use as behavior shaped by biology, trauma, environment, markets, and inequality."}, {"id": "984e82bc-29f4-48ef-a44c-fb7305eaa94d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policy responses and harm reduction", "children": [{"id": "1c1540b3-605d-4779-987a-70067b74773f", "type": "concept", "title": "Drug courts and diversion"}, {"id": "a115c215-16e5-47f2-a477-aa51014f3754", "type": "concept", "title": "Needle exchange and naloxone"}, {"id": "3a80c285-dd3b-47d4-af76-b4e2ca0d44e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Legalization and regulation"}], "description": "Students compare criminalization, decriminalization, treatment, prevention, and harm-reduction models."}]}, {"id": "1cb1f697-fbb6-450c-a37d-e5f3d422f7e3", "type": "topic", "title": "Sexuality, Bodies, and Boundary Regulation", "description": "Societies regulate sexuality, bodies, reproduction, intimacy, and gender presentation through law, medicine, religion, media, and everyday interaction. This unit examines who is marked deviant and why.", "children": [{"id": "5dc926a0-99d1-40d1-b554-82c471dfecd6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sexual norms and deviance", "children": [{"id": "fc76a844-6ea9-4437-bf0c-90ad75ba5e43", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent and harm"}, {"id": "1958b2ee-7223-4875-b5d7-4c3622189f63", "type": "concept", "title": "Sex work debates"}, {"id": "6b77c4a9-2dfb-448b-89fd-08014320908a", "type": "concept", "title": "Pornography and regulation"}], "description": "Students analyze shifting norms around sexuality, intimacy, consent, marriage, sex work, and pornography."}, {"id": "0ab2e052-4f57-45e4-a5d9-178d7d97630f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Body norms and bodily deviance", "children": [{"id": "25517081-e98e-4c33-9089-532c238e1416", "type": "concept", "title": "Body surveillance"}, {"id": "2350afb0-ed09-43c2-b5fc-cf054c39772d", "type": "concept", "title": "Fat stigma and health discourse"}, {"id": "b1731512-11f4-4f4c-8013-18bbadb96888", "type": "concept", "title": "Body modification"}], "description": "This subtopic examines body size, disability, appearance, illness, tattoos, modification, and beauty standards."}, {"id": "5b42bdbc-d7cf-4872-8056-0653d5b494fe", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reproduction and family regulation", "children": [{"id": "e0549c9b-6914-4bd3-becc-9006fbcf9dd2", "type": "concept", "title": "Reproductive governance"}, {"id": "c78c158d-de85-4d86-8f5d-b7c0bcd290a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Teen pregnancy and moral judgment"}, {"id": "de9455a5-c831-42c3-b2f3-baca02b73350", "type": "concept", "title": "Family diversity"}], "description": "Students explore how reproductive behavior, parenting, pregnancy, and family forms become sites of social control."}]}, {"id": "fb7717b6-55a5-4cc0-912d-ae7513c5e74d", "type": "topic", "title": "Youth, Schools, Families, and Delinquency", "description": "Youth deviance is often treated as both danger and vulnerability. This unit analyzes delinquency, school discipline, family regulation, peer culture, and the transition from informal correction to formal control.", "children": [{"id": "1a04f0e8-5ffb-4e6e-90bf-5c1cbd45d33c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Juvenile delinquency and development", "children": [{"id": "a3146639-a08e-4970-ba54-b1cfe23512c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer groups and status"}, {"id": "25303bf8-a479-4d4e-808f-92fc9cacc12d", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk and resilience"}, {"id": "8568d881-108a-4009-a3ee-29b26877c736", "type": "concept", "title": "Life-course perspectives"}], "description": "Students examine youth behavior through sociological, developmental, and institutional lenses."}, {"id": "1f247321-ebb5-4da9-9059-ed86c05f13c4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Schools as control institutions", "children": [{"id": "eb576a80-fca2-43f9-a02b-82a4828e2401", "type": "concept", "title": "Zero tolerance policies"}, {"id": "7d5163cb-4cf1-4ad0-afb7-96e93ff9a154", "type": "concept", "title": "School resource officers"}, {"id": "649b2232-207b-4c2e-8301-392b2cc91644", "type": "concept", "title": "Restorative school discipline"}], "description": "This subtopic studies discipline, surveillance, tracking, suspension, expulsion, and school-to-prison pipeline debates."}, {"id": "5f597ea0-1898-4584-b9ce-a1aa1e7d7ffc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Family regulation and child welfare", "children": [{"id": "9f9d20be-334c-4e4a-8f8f-beaafd70c23c", "type": "concept", "title": "Parenting norms"}, {"id": "08041a1e-775b-4521-8eb4-fa2b9ec2251f", "type": "concept", "title": "Child welfare systems"}, {"id": "6b6f3106-cd87-4afd-b4f3-9fd581e1709e", "type": "concept", "title": "Poverty and neglect categories"}], "description": "Students analyze how families are supported, blamed, monitored, or sanctioned."}]}, {"id": "87d0edd9-d738-49c8-a958-f1a6ccbf81c2", "type": "topic", "title": "Media, Moral Panics, Digital Platforms, and Public Narratives", "description": "Media shape which behaviors become visible, frightening, laughable, punishable, or normalized. This unit examines how deviance narratives circulate through news, entertainment, social media, and digital platforms.", "children": [{"id": "59290844-c0f9-4d44-a12d-e3da018dc91a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "News, entertainment, and crime narratives", "children": [{"id": "c26b3688-3f3a-4591-b8ad-e38ebd24d715", "type": "concept", "title": "Framing and agenda setting"}, {"id": "1f4ed451-044f-4095-94df-eccfe6a43668", "type": "concept", "title": "Fear of crime"}, {"id": "5e184b48-ed95-46bd-9467-181560bd6cc7", "type": "concept", "title": "True crime and spectacle"}], "description": "Students study how media frames crime, disorder, victims, offenders, and institutions."}, {"id": "20928a63-3824-4a5b-8214-c47a3d7e230d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Moral panics and folk devils", "children": [{"id": "c97c434f-0a60-4944-9a86-171820d2f547", "type": "concept", "title": "Folk devils"}, {"id": "bca798e7-f753-42b1-b6ed-f5a3ce309d50", "type": "concept", "title": "Disproportionality"}, {"id": "379b2b16-a6f5-492d-8e0c-4328dbb2c7ae", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy overreaction"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces the classic moral panic model and applies it to contemporary cases."}, {"id": "f2efa97f-f15b-4797-8a26-d1f909476369", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital deviance and platform control", "children": [{"id": "b00cb9a5-0b78-471a-82a2-a0a7b5b33ef0", "type": "concept", "title": "Platform rules"}, {"id": "f155f5f9-3ac9-49c8-9b9e-1168cf45aea2", "type": "concept", "title": "Content moderation"}, {"id": "392a0237-e9f0-4d64-857a-12e6c5e36f79", "type": "concept", "title": "Digital shaming and surveillance"}], "description": "Students analyze online harassment, hacking, misinformation, cancel culture, content moderation, and algorithmic governance."}]}, {"id": "e71c8ca6-a6de-4ea1-a10c-4d69ed093bdd", "type": "topic", "title": "Globalization, Transnational Deviance, and Comparative Social Control", "description": "Deviance and control are not confined to one society. This unit compares legal systems, punishment, migration control, transnational crime, human rights, and global moral campaigns.", "children": [{"id": "44801c76-5648-43a3-ae79-6061855968c9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparative deviance and law", "children": [{"id": "eb2106ed-ed69-4cf4-b144-2a1d4ae038c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Legal pluralism"}, {"id": "558fb889-9df0-44d1-9e3e-7579d2e6beaf", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural variation"}, {"id": "f4367aaa-f4f9-445c-9d0d-9f1f7e2ab1ed", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparative punishment"}], "description": "Students compare how societies classify drugs, sexuality, protest, religion, disorder, and punishment."}, {"id": "1ced7b2e-347a-4f8c-9594-4f7bbd4a0df4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Transnational crime and control", "children": [{"id": "a8894cc8-2212-484a-a9a5-2a089b2a2ae6", "type": "concept", "title": "Organized crime"}, {"id": "6f2bf7a4-38c5-42e0-9683-f8e05c20a4f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Border surveillance"}, {"id": "e01d99ac-90e4-4e0c-bb13-8d6a8b940048", "type": "concept", "title": "International enforcement networks"}], "description": "This subtopic examines trafficking, cybercrime, organized crime, terrorism, border control, and international policing."}, {"id": "3bfa5d21-6f84-458e-b535-1426dd770fb8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Human rights and state power", "children": [{"id": "fefab2f8-81c4-4758-affd-9a60fe8737b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Political repression"}, {"id": "2e8bd67a-8e98-43b2-8069-e97c3d93b470", "type": "concept", "title": "Prisons and detention"}, {"id": "e92e5337-c4e8-4926-bb5e-ce3f58a36635", "type": "concept", "title": "Human rights monitoring"}], "description": "Students analyze when social control becomes abuse and how global actors challenge state violence."}]}, {"id": "3e1da56a-186c-49bd-8829-21f0435d9443", "type": "topic", "title": "Capstone: Deviance Case Study, Evidence Portfolio, and Policy Brief", "description": "The course culminates with students applying theory and evidence to a deviance or social control case. The capstone asks them to connect concepts, data, lived experience, institutions, ethics, and policy choices.", "children": [{"id": "2a797485-938a-4ee4-887c-08a75620b9ad", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case selection and theoretical frame", "children": [{"id": "9a08884c-ab18-4447-bfa0-f93a834f1ffb", "type": "concept", "title": "Research question"}, {"id": "9a84455f-c099-43b9-b1b5-f0e36956d3a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Theory map"}, {"id": "ee7215d7-b469-4fe2-b41b-7d88a24e34a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Scope and definitions"}], "description": "Students choose a case and explain which theories best illuminate it."}, {"id": "8572888d-c433-44d3-bcf1-71dbb1c47808", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence portfolio", "children": [{"id": "1f3a4e51-5de2-4d7b-9e1b-14f86039b2ae", "type": "concept", "title": "Official statistics or datasets"}, {"id": "e6125647-bc9b-4704-a169-492cee2236be", "type": "concept", "title": "Scholarly literature"}, {"id": "b746c657-0f66-4d86-a867-564af9d12933", "type": "concept", "title": "Media, policy, or interview evidence"}], "description": "This subtopic requires students to combine scholarly sources, data, policy documents, and qualitative evidence."}, {"id": "e01be272-827e-4299-a7ec-660725b7106b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policy brief and public presentation", "children": [{"id": "975a731a-a97e-4314-9926-7c8f0d6473ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Problem definition"}, {"id": "c8976133-acba-4ac2-b118-ed1dee35d63e", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy options"}, {"id": "35c9828e-2933-4449-94cb-c5c6bb4cb620", "type": "concept", "title": "Limitations and ethical tradeoffs"}], "description": "Students translate analysis into a concise, evidence-based recommendation or critique."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$devsjson$::jsonb,
  true,
